  "definition": "William James Dally (born August 17, 1960) is an American computer scientist and educator.",
  "details": "Spearheaded tensor cores, NVLink high-speed interconnects, and low-precision floating-point formats (FP8/FP4) that multiplied GPU AI performance by orders of magnitude. He is the chief scientist and senior vice president at Nvidia and was previously a professor of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science at Stanford University and MIT. Since 2021, he has been a member of the President's Council of Advisors on Science and Technology (PCAST).",
